      "title": "bin/interlock is 173 bytes under the package-size test's ceiling",
      "description": "The file is 245,587 bytes against the 245,760-byte limit test/spine/package.test.mjs enforces (256 KiB less 16 KiB headroom). The design (D3) kept logic in lib/ to protect this, but the next change that touches the binary, even a usage line, will fail the package test and have to move code out first.",
      "suggestion": "Move one more block of argument parsing or usage text out of bin/interlock into lib/ now, or record in the follow-up that the next binary edit starts with a size-recovery task.",
