    },
    {
      "dimension": "technical-lead",
      "severity": "suggestion",
      "file": "lib/merge-confidence.mjs",
      "line": 247,
      "title": "A scoped, carried re-review reads in the verdict as a narrow review",
      "description": "After D18 the final review record of a settle pass may have ran = only reReviewDimensions, with the rest carried. readReviewRan prints depth but neither the carried count nor that the review was scoped, and the 'every selected dimension ran' green is trivially true when selected equals the scoped set. A reader of a MERGE verdict cannot tell the whole pull request was not re-examined. The design says the depth in evidence lets a reader ask for --strict, but the carry is the other half of that fact.",
      "suggestion": "When review.counts.carried is positive, push an evidence line such as 'carried: <n> finding(s) from dimensions not re-run'. Evidence only, no band, consistent with D20.",
      "votes": {
        "real": 0,
        "notReal": 0,
        "uncited": 0,
        "total": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "dimension": "blast-radius",
      "severity": "warning",
      "file": "skills/settle/SKILL.md",
      "line": 246,
      "title": "fixer-result re-derives deferrals from a profile the skill marks optional",
      "description": "settle-cli.mjs briefedRound now defers protected-path and previously-declined findings before planning, and fixerResultCommand calls it with protectionFor(). The skill's remediate-brief call (line 218) passes --profile profile-r<r>.json, but its fixer-result call (line 246) lists --profile and --previous as optional. Without them fixer-result falls back to the default profile path (protectionFor, settle-cli.mjs:343) and a different deferral set, so its briefed id set can differ from the one the fixer was given. Before the change fixer-result planned from the whole record and no profile was involved, so any caller that omits the flags (the old argv still parses) now sees a partition mismatch or a refusal.",
      "suggestion": "Make --profile and --previous required for fixer-result whenever the brief used them, or have remediate-brief persist the deferred ids in its result so fixer-result reads them rather than recomputing. Pin the flags in test/skills.test.mjs.",
      "votes": {
        "real": 2,
        "notReal": 0,
        "uncited": 0,
        "total": 2
      },
      "qualityScores": [
        3,
        4
      ]
    },
    {
      "dimension": "blast-radius",
      "severity": "suggestion",
      "file": "lib/merge-confidence.mjs",
      "line": 194,
      "title": "Carried findings reach merge-confidence as ordinary surviving findings",
      "description": "carryForward (review-core.mjs) appends findings from an earlier head into result.surviving, so counts.surviving and the record's surviving list now include them. merge-confidence readReview (line 191-194) and settle-cli survivingOf (line 173) read that list and treat carried findings like fresh ones. The carried: true marker is only read by settle replies. Their file:line locators refer to the earlier head and may be stale. The band behaviour is consistent with the design, but nothing in merge-confidence names the carried count.",
      "suggestion": "Surface counts.carried in merge-confidence evidence next to depth, or note in a test that carried findings count toward the band by design.",
